{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/125778-many-ideas-what-to-develope","id":125778,"title":"Many ideas- what to develope?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-05T07:18:34-07:00","id":125778,"title":"Many ideas- what to develope?","content":"So, I have a number of different ideas for hunter organizations (for some I didn't even decided on their Tier). My basic premise is making one per gameline, with few &quot;generalized&quot; organizations- except of the Sin Eaters, for they already have the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/38053-dying-conspiracy-ebony-fangs\" target=\"_blank\">Ebony Fangs</a> (I'm not including <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/16573-conspiracy-raziel-ltd-wip\">Raziel</a> as the &quot;demon hunters&quot;, although their obvious connection to the God Machine and the mysteries about their CEO- for the definition for Empyrean Phenomena is a lot wider than that). So, I've decided to present those ideas in short in here, and to start working on the most popular idea (not that I won't work on the others eventually- but just to see what is more wanted in here).<br /> <br /> In short- here are the ideas!<br /> <br /> Nimrod's Children- a group of hunters who believe that no greater power should rule humanity's fate. Most of them are atheists, believing the many &quot;gods&quot; are just powerful creatures who seek to use humans as their pawns, while others believe in the power of higher beings, but wish that humanity will be free to decide its own fate. They name themselves after Nimrod, the first man to rebel against God. If they have an Endowment, it would be the Enochian Whispers- the ability to command the little angels which are found inside reality to force their will upon heaven and earth.<br /> <br /> The Pythonians Oracles- descended from the Oracle of Delphi, each of them was chosen to deliver a better future by a primordial power from before time. They are prophets and fortune tellers, driven by the so called &quot;Vision&quot; to create a new, better world, where there is no darkness. The one to give them their &quot;prophet&quot; is often named as the chatonic serpent Python, yet no one knows that for sure. While they may seem as only a Conspiracy, they could work as a compact- if you decide that the only one with the powers of prophesy is their mad leader, the nameless Oracle.<br /> <br /> Queen Anne\u2019s Reveng- named after the ship of the notorious pirate Edward Thatch, they hail from the Golden Age of Piracy. Yet, as piracy fell from its grace, they found other ways to adept to the new world. By using their knowledge about buried treasures, lore gained from the &quot;heretics&quot; and connections with &quot;friends from higher places&quot;, they managed to survive to the modern world. They still see themselves as &quot;pirates&quot;, although most of them don't go on ships anymore- and some are even &quot;internet pirates&quot;. If they have Endowments, then they may be similar in nature to the AKD- but their &quot;relics&quot; work only on certain places, with more powerful the &quot;treasure&quot; more rare is the location.<br /> <br /> Caretakers of the Dark Mother- the first specialized group, they are the vampire hunters. They descend from heretic sects which worshiped Lilith for the protection she granted against vampires and similar abominations. They see her as the mother of all vampires, and the bloodsuckers as her renegade children. However, they also know that her other children- the shadowy owls named Lilin- also roam the night, and those children also rebel against the will of their mother after losing the purpose she granted them years ago- and like any good mother, she wants to educate them. If they have and Endowment, it would be the ability to shape shadows.<br /> <br /> Sora no Akatsuki- &quot;the Empty Dawn&quot; (at least, I hope that it means that), they are the &quot;new onmyoji&quot;- people who seek to reestablish the old faith and power of the <i>onmy\u014dd\u014d</i> in the modern age. They are the &quot;spirit hunters&quot;, and they seek to bind the powers of the lower spirits to serve their organization and their nation. While there are few who dream about the creation of a new imperial rule, they are minority, with the most seek to adept their faith and techniques to the modern world. They are either a group of modernists who seek power in the old traditions (which could make them into a compact), decendents of the old onmyoji families (which may turn them into a Conspiracy) or both. Their Endowment, if they have one, will be based around summoning and controlling shikigami through virtual reality and hi tech (see the &quot;empty&quot; part of their name)<br /> <br /> Museum of Mysteries- an occult society dedicated to the hunt of magic. They seek after the very essence of magical powers, and collect the most horrifying and magnificent discoveries into their own &quot;museums&quot; and &quot;zoos&quot;. They are philosophers, and they focus their efforts after witches and &quot;enlighten magic&quot; in order to find a way to share their power (after all, witches are almost human- so what makes them different enough to be able to use their powers?). While they claim to have no other agenda but &quot;collecting magic for the beauty of its wonders&quot;, not all buy to that agenda- after all, no one is going to collect so much magic just to &quot;watch it&quot;. Their Endowments, if they have one, would be based around &quot;hitch-hiking&quot; the connection that witch's and similar magical powers to the Source in order to work some weird magic of their own.<br /> <br /> The Ashen Collective- a group which seeks after the secrets of life and death, they focus their efforts around the Divine Fire as the source of limitless potential. They track down prometheans, but not only- actually, pandorans are seen as even more interesting, for unlike the first their energy is for &quot;static&quot;, and as such could be kept under control better than the more &quot;wild&quot; energy of the prometheans- hence the &quot;Ashen&quot; in their name. Their dream is to capture a qasmal, which would give them an animated &quot;piece&quot; of Divine Fire. They are mostly intellectual group, but they aren't scared to get their hands dirty in order to find the mythical &quot;philosopher stone&quot;. If they are a Conspiracy, their Endowments would work as &quot;reactive devices&quot;- something like the pandorans. They are usually asleep, yet they awaken at certain times. Divine Fire always awakes them, but there are also under things which would make them work.<br /> <br /> Cantores Fati- people who believe that the world could be a better place, if they would be the ones to tell its story. They seek after the powers of Fate, and as such, the Fae, in order to make sure that there would always be an &quot;happy ending&quot; like in legends- even if the happy ending would be preety gruesome for the antagonists. According to their world view, there is little to no difference between reality and a story, it is just that humanity forgot how to tell the story they wish to hear. Their problem with the Fair Folk is that they sometimes use their powers in order to create different stories than the Singers wish to tell, and so sometimes their voices need to be.. silenced. They are, however, open for bargains with certain faeries, if they'll support their own vision of how a story would need to &quot;end&quot;. The Endowments, if they'll have any, would be something similar to Talecrafting, with a certain Singer needs to sing or tell how things are going to happen in order to make Fate do his will.<br /> <br /> Movers of the Heart- a group of people who has found a powerful Relic ages ago, named the Heart of Lost Heavens. They believes the Relic to be sacred, and that they must protect it from the hands of the self proclaimed &quot;god kings&quot;. The Heart is a broken Relic, and each of it's pieces is hidden by another headquarter of the group. No one knows to how many pieces the Heart has been broken, but one thing is known- that bad things may happen if a mummy would get its hand upon one of its parts. In order to keep the Heart safe, and to protect themselves from its Curses, the Heart must be moved according to a sacred geomancy, and breaking of that geomancy may create some... unfortunate side effects. They may gain weird powers from the Heart (if they are a Conspiracy), which would work by using the Heart's geomancy in order to create certain effects.<br /> <br /> Project Troja- a group which believes that the God Machine is some kind of a defense mechanism made by the makes of the world, and so it should be supported. Yet, they think that the God Machine lacks direction, and as such they should find a way to &quot;hack&quot; it and make sure that someone would direct its actions for the benefit of mankind. For that reason, they search after demons and similar rouge/ stolen parts of the God Machine, modify them and &quot;return them&quot; back to the God Machine as some sort of &quot;trojan horses&quot;. In a way, they are a &quot;cancer cult&quot; inside the God Machine's mortal believers. If they have the resources of a conspiracy, than they have an Endowment- the ability to sacrifice (or &quot;give back&quot;) a part of the God Machine back to it, and in return make it to do something for them- even in a small, insignificant way.<br /> <br /> La Tempesta- as a bonus, here are some infernal &quot;demon hunters&quot;. They use the idea that certain demons are defined by their myths and testaments, and so they seek to bind them into the poetry, acting and arts. All of them are artists, and they agree that while Vice is not inherently wrong, it should be supervised and control through the force of art. Their motto is &quot;Hell is Empty, and all the Devils are Here!&quot;- meaning that the world in a bad place by its essence, and you can at best to navigate through the Tempest until you'll find your &quot;safe island&quot;, and what is better than fighting evil with evil? While it may make them vulnerable against their own inner demons (and some of them even allow themselves to be temporary Possessed by them), those with a virtue strong enough could find their way home. If they are a conspiracy, than their Endowments should be able to channel demons through characters made by Shakespeare's many plays.<br /> <br /> so- here are them! Which ideas are good? Which need to be refined? Any constructive feedback is welcomed <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 05-05-2014, 04:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T10:37:02-07:00","id":126788,"title":"","content":"So... anyone?... Anyone?....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T14:57:21-07:00","id":138420,"title":"","content":"so because of the lack of input, I think I may do the Oracles next- while Nimrod's Children are in the back of my mind for a long time (one of the original 4 conspiracy ideas I had, with the other three being Raziel, the Fangs and another conspiracy which has shared too much with the newly Faithful) , the Oracles came soon after them (inspired from a Slasher conspiracy I once made, saying the truth. I may even make them into a Slasher conspiracy, but of a different type), and I kinda have a muse for them right now- so watch for them!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T12:07:23-07:00","id":284019,"title":"","content":"Nimrod's Children are pretty compelling. I would be very interested in seeing how you work out their Endowments. Way I see it, it could either be that the spirits are relic-like in the sense that they are each relatively unique to some degree (as opposed to the VALKYRIE endowments) or simply a pile up of effects similar to Castigation or Benediction. Either of those would keep my attention.<br /> <br /> The Empty Dawn are interesting as well, but I feel they have too much in common with the NC. <br /> <br /> Queen Anne's Revenge is a bit flat. I could see them as a cell more than anything else. Same goes for La Temptesta. <br /> <br /> The Cantores Fati are another one that I would like to see in deeper detail. I feel this faction has no choice but to be a conspiracy, and were that the case, I would enjoy seeing them work like Castigation or Benediction. As an org I think they would do well to serve as the Changeling and True Fae specialists that I've felt was lacking for a while.<br /> <br /> The Museum of Mysteries... I don't think it would work too well. Breaking confinement as an Awakened is just too easy.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4105-reverendgrene","name":"Reverendgrene","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T12:39:04-07:00","id":284051,"title":"","content":"i would go with Nimrods Children.<br /> <br /> EDIT: oh and the Queen Anne's Revenge, just because I like pirates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":3742,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","user":"Iceblade44","date":". 10-16-2014, 07:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T15:53:36-07:00","id":284303,"title":"","content":"In my personal opinion, I would vote for Nimrod's Children, the Empty Dawn, and the Ashen Collective on the virtue that they are effectively fighting against the antagonists of Demon, Werewolf, and Promethean, respectively <i>(though the Ashen Collective is more of a grey area and spirits aren't necessarily the opposing force of Werewolf)</i>. I'm also enjoying Cantores Fati for the delicious fluff. <br /> <br /> Nimrod's Children - I find that their driving force is definitely strong, considering that it appears that they have no ulterior motive than to remove humanity from the influence of divine beings. However, I find the Enochian Whispers to work against their directive; if they want to remove divine influence, why are they using angels within reality? Is there a way for them to focus on the accomplishments of man as acts of Divine Defiance or Rebellion?<br /> <br /> The Empty Dawn - As an Asian-American, I find that the inclusion of a Japanese-based organization is wonderful. The fact that the group focuses on &quot;spirit-hunters&quot; also leads my mind into the <i>Fatal Frame</i> series (although that series focuses on Shinto). However, I would like to say that you would want to be careful about representing this group; despite the Canon Conspiracies involving certain cultures and religions, I feel that some individuals will be critical over this organization. I still feel that this Conspiracy is one that'll be needed.<br /> <br /> The Ashen Collective - Conceptually, I am divided on this Conspiracy. On one hand, they are searching the truth behind life and death and are harvesting pieces of the Divine Fire, mainly from Pandorans. That's cool. On the other hand, I don't feel as interested in the organization. They are intellectuals that want to know about life and death; what else is there to know? They seem too normal to be part of the World of Darkness, which runs the gamut of movie-esque hardened warriors that punch demons to the Inquisition. I would like something to sink my teeth into for this group.<br /> <br /> Cantores Fati - YES. <b><i>YES.</i></b> I love the storytelling motif that blends with the mood of <i>Changeling</i>. Despite being rather otherworldly <i>(like, Final Fantasy-level of otherworldly)</i>, the theme of rewriting fate is one that I would love to see being explored a bit more in NWoD, where it seems that the future is always going to be dark.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1417-reaper-verse","name":"Reaper Verse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T10:13:16-07:00","id":285995,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">WHO HAS AWAKEN ME FROM MY SLEE-</span></b> oh, its you guys.<br /> <br /> Actually, I even forgot that this thread exist. Anyway, yeah, I must agree that Nimrod's Children are my most developed (and apparently, best accepted) idea. I also like the Empty Dawn and the Cantores Fati, and it also reminds me I should write the Oracle's Endowment (plus, there is a project I may start which should include some new conspiracy/compact ideas)<br /> <br /> That, and finishing Conjurer.. and writing the Old Ones.. so much to do...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T14:23:53-07:00","id":286180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nimrod's Children - I find that their driving force is definitely strong, considering that it appears that they have no ulterior motive than to remove humanity from the influence of divine beings. However, I find the Enochian Whispers to work against their directive; if they want to remove divine influence, why are they using angels within reality? Is there a way for them to focus on the accomplishments of man as acts of Divine Defiance or Rebellion? </div> </div> </div>Fighting holy fire with holy fire. Besides, one may guess there are few things which can piss God as much as forcing HIS angels to disobey HIM and bow to mortals\u00b4 whims.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","user":"Raistlin","date":". 10-19-2014, 06:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T14:49:00-07:00","id":286187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/125778-many-ideas-what-to-develope?p=286180#post286180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fighting holy fire with holy fire. Besides, one may guess there are few things which can piss God as much as forcing HIS angels to disobey HIM to bow to mortals\u00b4 whims.</div> </div> </div> </div>yep- plus, they have a very technical way to treat those &quot;lesser angels&quot;, seeing them more as &quot;forces of nature&quot; which could be commanded with the right words (similar to how a thaumaturge Obrimos would see the &quot;divine&quot;). Angels, after all, are not the &quot;higher power&quot;, but the messengers with which the higher power manifest its will. Control the angels, and their god will be powerless, while man will be the new god (at least, that's how they see things)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T15:21:18-07:00","id":286206,"title":"","content":"Also, the chances are that the Ashen Collective and the La Tempesta will be devoured alive by a project I'm planning- creating hunter orgs based on Ascension's (withe the former being absorbed into the &quot;Solifacti&quot; while the later to the &quot;Wu Keng&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T23:16:35-07:00","id":287284,"title":"","content":"I'm porting stuff from Ascension too, just I remove Awakened element and twists groups to something different ultimately.<br /> <br /> Hedgewalkers (modern setting) / Voyagers (space opera setting of mine): There are places humans wishes to reach just because they are there, and Hedge is no exception. Group of mavericks and occultists who through deals with Changelings and their own brand of non-Awakened sorceries developed means to ward-off influence of Hedge on mortal travelers, but exploring it they stumbled on terrific truth that there are inscrutable monsters which toy with humans. But they did not back off, just found a worthy purpose. Shield mortals and those who escaped from the clutches of Gentry as best as they can. Basically now anti-Gentry focused Conspiracy, they joined forces with Courts (especially Summer Court) and bonds of comradeship were forged in fire between those eccentric mortals and Changelings. In space opera setting in which Hedge was discovered by mortal scientists as means of FTL travel, they came out of shadow and served as intermediaries between the interstellar government and their Changeling allies, freeholds and Hedgewalkers (renamed Voyagers now) monopolizing interstellar travel. Basically, they are Void Engineers with a twist of being bedfellows with supernaturals (Beast Kiths are fine too, ask Carlos McConnell). And darker Starfleet of Star Trek but with Changelings instead of Federation allied aliens.<br /> <br /> Feel free to use this semi-homebrew. I'm also porting New World Order as Conspiracy with closer ties to some of Agencies of Descent (seeking to remake the world into one where humanity is free to carve out its own destiny without God-Machine or Gentry meddling. They are willing to cooperate with those Demons whose visions of global Hell without GM has humanity's interests in mind. They have some relationship with Changelings, but not to the same extent as Hedgewalkers). Daedalians, being Iteration X's equivalent, find occult physics of God-Machine fascinating field of research, and aim to one day to be able reverse-engineer Infrastructure, but so far they were only able to do that with some Embeds (put into Devices they use as their Endowments). They are also fascinated with Prometheans in very wrong way. They are not truly demiurges, but thinks Pyros might be a key to advance them on the path of another goal which is creation of true AI. They dream of creating robotic constructs that are more stable, predictable and are not deluded to discard away their nature. Prometheans only serve as convenient Pyros source and nothing more. Daedalians are basically those colleagues you find creepy and not too sympathetic, but the alliance of Hedgewalkers and New World Order finds them too convenient to kick out of the group (in far future they provide Rip Gate imbued Devices for voidships, and their other Devices are invaluable too).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":2918,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","user":"Kat","date":". 10-20-2014, 02:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}